      "title": "Module Introduction",
      "sourceHash": "af8185d93dfcc56eb893c7c928f5102b6422f978efeac2b57241d35aa55fa0a1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.33,
          "end": 4.45,
          "en": "In this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.45,
          "end": 5.87,
          "en": "we are going to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.87,
          "end": 9.14,
          "en": "how we may build components in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.14,
          "end": 11.29,
          "en": "Well, wait a second!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.29,
          "end": 13.04,
          "en": "Isn't that something we've learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.04,
          "end": 15.54,
          "en": "in-depth until now already?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 19.03,
          "en": "Well we did, but there is an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.03,
          "end": 21.11,
          "en": "of building components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.11,
          "end": 24.49,
          "en": "Besides building components as functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.49,
          "end": 26.9,
          "en": "which is what we did up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.9,
          "end": 31.13,
          "en": "you can also define components with classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.13,
          "end": 34.33,
          "en": "You can build Class-based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.33,
          "end": 37.03,
          "en": "But I get one important note, right away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.03,
          "end": 39.15,
          "en": "before you feel overwhelmed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.15,
          "end": 42.88,
          "en": "This is 100% optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.88,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "and in most modern React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "you are probably not going to use this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.68,
          "en": "You can therefore skip this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.68,
          "end": 57.47,
          "en": "but I wanna emphasize that you will see a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.47,
          "end": 61.18,
          "en": "of Class-based Components out there, in the wild,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.18,
          "end": 64.3,
          "en": "in third-party libraries or in projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.3,
          "end": 68.14,
          "en": "you might be working on, because traditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.14,
          "end": 69.72,
          "en": "not too long ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.72,
          "end": 74.53,
          "en": "you had to use Class-based Components in certain cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.53,
          "end": 76.16,
          "en": "This is no longer the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.16,
          "end": 80.15,
          "en": "but I will explain all about that throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.15,
          "end": 83.71000000000001,
          "en": "I will explain what exactly Class-based Components are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.71000000000001,
          "end": 86.36,
          "en": "and why they exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.36,
          "end": 89.56,
          "en": "We will learn how we can build Class-based Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.56,
          "end": 92.84,
          "en": "and how we can work with Class-based Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.84,
          "end": 95.97,
          "en": "and, we're then also going to have a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.97,
          "end": 99.89,
          "en": "Error Boundaries, and at least this is something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.89,
          "end": 103.44,
          "en": "you should at least take a mental note to come back to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.44,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "because Error Boundaries, right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 110.58,
          "en": "require Class-based Components to be built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 112.75999999999999,
          "en": "That being said, you will not build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.75999999999999,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "a lot of Error Boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 118.87,
          "en": "But still, this module holds important information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.87,
          "end": 122.4,
          "en": "about React's past, about an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.4,
          "end": 123.81,
          "en": "of building components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 125.56,
          "en": "and most importantly of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 128.603,
          "en": "why that way exists and how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
